{
  "build": "1.9.35, 03.10.2026: source-only пакет. Для FM+ STAT/PAR/DYN сохранены шесть selectable FRQ/BPM renderer IDs 0..5; historical raw IDs 6..8 normalised в MNM FRQ. Schema 42 снимает неработающий DLY CORE из menu/runtime/shipping Source: selector снова mnm|old|new, а saved CORE value 3 из schema 40/41 мигрирует в NEW=2. Schema 44 добавляет persisted DFB BASE CURVE и HOLD @64: RAW=63 — reference, RAW 0..63 идёт по editable curve, RAW=64 получает небольшой hold, а RAW 65+ сохраняет RAW/64 growth. Fresh BASE defaults: CURVE=.55, HOLD@64=.9920. Для schema <44 migration намеренно добавляет CURVE=1 и HOLD@64=1, точно сохраняя старый RAW/64 state. RAW <=63 остаётся guard bypass, RAW 63..64 — soft arm, RAW 64..127 интерполирует четыре GUARD LVL anchor (START/PLT @64 и @127) с общим OFFSET. Fresh GUARD defaults: START@64=0, PLT@64=.05, START@127=0, PLT@127=3.46, OFFSET=.18, CURVE=1.08, AMOUNT=2, ATTACK=1 ms, RELEASE=1 ms; DYNAMICS, оба DSND FB INVERT, RETURN COMP и FB CLIP ON. Guard 65x257 LUT и BASE LUT rebuild только при реальном изменении sanitized snapshot, не при каждом audio block. DFB RMB panel — white 400x386 pinned child overlay внутри VST, без X, native OS window и edge jitter; repaint 10 Hz. Schema-39 anchors и schema-40 raw GUARD ID остаются для безопасной загрузки state. DBAS/DWID 12 dB response, CHOR Native/Core, FM и Phaser contracts не менялись. Выполнен только static audit; full build, VST3/DAW, render и executable tests не заявляются. ARP UI follow-up: redundant PAGE 1..64 canvas caption removed, SONG toggle text label hidden while its control/tooltip remains, COPY/PASTE first popup item is WHOLE PAGE, and all PluginEditor function tooltip payloads use English/ASCII because the pixel tooltip font cannot display Cyrillic. MOD ENV UI follow-up: held-LMB crossing between AMP/FIL/MOD categories now commits selection atomically; compact MOD ENV uses the AMP/FIL 387x236 shell and control grid, without its former MATRIX/RMB/page-route mini labels. MOD ENV1..4 selection and ROUTE TO remain on the retained RMB large page. Schema 45: each P1/P2 direct LFO owns persistent UNI/BI, INV and ALT DUAL; fresh DPTH is 0, normal range 0..127 and ALT DUAL opens -127..+127. P2 direct DEST uses target-local offsets instead of raw target modulo; MOD MATRIX adds rN_inv, two collapsible INTERNAL LFO groups and hover target preview. Legacy direct DPTH values are intentionally reset to 0 during schema-45 migration. LFO timing correction restores final TRIG=HALF (raw 4) for all independent P1/P2 LFO groups: it restarts at phase 0, stops exactly at half cycle and retains its final output. SPD is now linear and tempo-relative with MULT=1X..64X: full-cycle 1/16 steps = 2048/(SPD*MULT), cycles/s = BPM*SPD*MULT/30720; the former exponential SPD curve is removed. Only source/static audit was run. LFO faceplate correction keeps PAGE/DEST target-local values at readable pixel scale, moves/enlarges the P1/P2 side badge, and anchors WAVE/choice popups to the originating cell using global screen bounds; no visual runtime render was run. Dynamic LFO SPD hover tooltip uses currentBpm() for live BPM plus active SPD/MULT; it reports 1/16, seconds, Hz, HALF and 2048/(SPD*MULT), guards SPD=0, updates with cache at UI 20 Hz, and remains English/ASCII; no visual runtime render was run. LFO LOCKS second PAGE column now reserves a non-selectable English/ASCII P2 PITCH N/A spacer; visible rows 1..10 still map exactly to PAGE 11..20, so lock/solo/state/routing and all 21 choices remain unchanged. Windows MSVC feedback found JUCE 8 C2665 on four legacy PopupMenu addCustomItem calls; they now use a PopupMenu::Item helper preserving custom hover preview, enabled/ticked state and IDs. No post-fix Windows build is claimed; rerun Release x64 VST3 is the next gate. Matrix corrective feedback: direct-LFO DPTH uses the original PAN-equivalent centred 52x43 rotary geometry and full centred LCD strip, while UNI/INV stay relative to that unchanged knob and never consume its LCD width. Direct P1-LFO DEST faceplate now reduces an already P1-prefix-compacted bank/LFO name (AMP PORT or LFO1 DPTH) to its leaf control (PORT or DPTH); dropdowns, LOCKS and Matrix names/IDs stay unchanged. Only redundant P1-on-P1 text is compacted; P2 badge/canonical names remain visible in faceplate popup/locks/Matrix. P2 AMP DIST/VOL/PAN use IDs 144/145/146. Matrix SOURCE names use P1/P2 LFO without `INTERNAL`; readable DEPTH/POLAR widths and `POLAR` header are restored. Bottom-pinned MatrixLfoDock has a white divider and P1/P2 PARAM/LFO PAGE folders. Fresh/clear/target-picked routes are ON but DEPTH=0/DEST=OFF remain inert; MSEG/patchcord allocation chooses an unlocked blank payload before legacy disabled rows. RESET ALL queues only changed APVTS values in ordered 12-notification async chunks after one undo snapshot; host-visible value notifications are retained, undo/redo waits for completion and editor destruction flushes a pending queue. Matrix/RESET verification is source-only; no post-change build, runtime UI, VST3/DAW, DSP test or render is claimed.",
